NeuroClaw
=========

NeuroClaw is a hard fork of PicoClaw v0.3.1 (https://github.com/sipeed/picoclaw,
tag v0.3.1, commit 2cf030d2), made for NeuroEdge (https://github.com/letrongminh/neuroedge-init).

PicoClaw is Copyright (c) 2026 PicoClaw contributors and released under the MIT License.
NeuroClaw keeps that license for all code, original and new; see LICENSE.

What NeuroClaw changes, and why, is in README.md ("What changed from PicoClaw").

NeuroClaw-ESP (esp32/)
----------------------

The C brain for one ESP32-S3 adapts the Telegram long-poll and chat-completions
clients of zclaw (https://github.com/tnm/zclaw, commit e3ad271), Copyright (c)
2026 Ted Nyman, MIT License; full text in esp32/LICENSE-zclaw. Its agent loop and
GPIO tools are not used: every action goes through the host firmware's gate.
cJSON (MIT, Dave Gamble) comes with ESP-IDF; the host tests fetch the same
v1.7.18 sources.
